UnitMetaquoter::quoteExactOutput
├── when the path is empty
│   └── it reverts with EP
└── given the path is not empty
    ├── when a pool factory is not approved
    │   └── it reverts with AF
    └── given the pool factory is approved
        ├── when the pool is not a registered target
        │   └── it reverts with IP
        └── given the pool is a registered target
            ├── when tokenIn is not a token of its hop pool
            │   └── it reverts with TI
            └── given tokenIn is a token of its hop pool
                ├── when the route is a single CL pool
                │   ├── it sizes the hop input from the exact output
                │   └── it populates the lists at the pool index
                ├── when the route has multiple CL hops
                │   ├── it sizes each hop input backward from the exact output
                │   ├── it populates the lists at each index
                │   └── it returns the first hop input as amountIn
                ├── when the route is a single V2 pool
                │   ├── it returns the getAmountInWithTotalFee quote
                │   └── it leaves the lists zeroed at the pool index
                ├── when the route mixes CL and V2 hops
                │   ├── it sizes each hop input backward through both pool kinds
                │   ├── it populates only the CL entries
                │   └── it returns the first hop input as amountIn
                ├── when a pool reports an unknown pool type
                │   ├── it does not read the factory pause flag
                │   ├── it does not read the pool tokens
                │   └── it reverts with PT
                └── when a V2 hop quotes zero input
                    └── it reverts with II

UnitMetaquoter::quoteExactInputSingleV2
├── when the pool factory is not approved
│   └── it reverts with AF
└── given the pool factory is approved
    ├── when the pool is not a registered target
    │   └── it reverts with IP
    └── given the pool is a registered target
        ├── when the pool type is not a V2 type
        │   └── it reverts with PT
        └── given the pool type is a V2 type
            ├── when the pool factory is paused
            │   └── it reverts with PS
            ├── when tokenIn is not a pool token
            │   └── it reverts with TI
            └── given tokenIn is a pool token
                ├── when the pool is V2 stable
                │   └── it returns the getAmountOutWithTotalFee quote
                ├── when the pool is V2 volatile
                │   └── it returns the getAmountOutWithTotalFee quote
                └── when the pool quotes zero output
                    └── it reverts with IO

UnitMetaquoter::quoteExactOutputSingleV2
├── when the pool factory is not approved
│   └── it reverts with AF
└── given the pool factory is approved
    ├── when the pool is not a registered target
    │   └── it reverts with IP
    └── given the pool is a registered target
        ├── when the pool type is not a V2 type
        │   └── it reverts with PT
        └── given the pool type is a V2 type
            ├── when the pool factory is paused
            │   └── it reverts with PS
            ├── when tokenIn is not a pool token
            │   └── it reverts with TI
            └── given tokenIn is a pool token
                ├── when the pool is V2 stable
                │   └── it returns the getAmountInWithTotalFee quote
                ├── when the pool is V2 volatile
                │   └── it returns the getAmountInWithTotalFee quote
                └── when the pool quotes zero input
                    └── it reverts with II

UnitMetaquoter::uniswapV3SwapCallback
├── when both deltas are non positive
│   └── it reverts with ZL
└── given a positive delta
    ├── when the caller is not the encoded pool
    │   └── it reverts with MS
    └── given the caller is the encoded pool
        ├── given an exact input simulation
        │   ├── when the input token is token0
        │   │   └── it reverts with the received amount and the pool price and tick
        │   └── when the input token is token1
        │       └── it reverts with the received amount and the pool price and tick
        └── given an exact output simulation
            ├── when no output is expected
            │   └── it reverts with the payable amount and the pool price and tick
            └── given an output is expected
                ├── when the received amount differs from the expected output
                │   └── it reverts with OC
                └── when the received amount matches the expected output
                    └── it reverts with the payable amount and the pool price and tick
